## 4. Data model changes (additive, lock-safe migrations)

The sketches below show intent. Adapt names to the existing schema and document the final DDL in the PR.

**Lock safety.** `calls` is hot: UTel writes to it all day.
- Never add a `GENERATED … STORED` column or an immediately-validated constraint to it. Both rewrite or scan the table under an exclusive lock.
- Add CHECK constraints as `NOT VALID` and `VALIDATE` them later. Validation takes a weaker lock.
- Run DDL after 23:00 Tashkent. Build indexes with `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY`.

```sql
-- 4.1 calls: new columns (all nullable or with constant defaults, so no table rewrite)
ALTER TABLE calls
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS local_day          date,          -- Tashkent date of the call's start time
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS local_hour         smallint,      -- 0..23 Tashkent
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS reason_key         text,          -- Appendix A.5 key, or internal 'unknown'
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS score10            numeric(3,1),  -- maintained by trigger from the 0–100 score column
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS client_phone_rev   text,          -- reversed digits, for fast suffix search
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS peaks              smallint[],    -- 200 values 0..100
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS peaks_status       text,          -- 'ok' | 'failed' | null
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS peaks_attempts     smallint NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS transcript_segments jsonb,        -- [{speaker,start,end,text}] when STT returns segments
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS audio_path         text,          -- storage key of the MP3 we control
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS audio_bytes        integer,
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS wav_path           text,          -- storage key of a kept WAV original, if any
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS wav_bytes          integer,
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS audio_received_at  timestamptz,   -- when the audio file reached us (arrival)
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS provider_audio_url text,          -- only for audio hosted solely at the telephony provider
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS retention_released_at timestamptz, -- set only by scripts/retention-held.mjs --release
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS audio_state        text NOT NULL DEFAULT 'available',
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS audio_trash_path   text,
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS wav_trash_path     text,
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS audio_trashed_at   timestamptz,
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS audio_removed_at   timestamptz,
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS audio_keep         boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS audio_keep_by      uuid,
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS audio_keep_at      timestamptz;
ALTER TABLE calls ADD CONSTRAINT calls_audio_state_chk
  CHECK (audio_state IN ('available','trashing','trashed','expired','missing')) NOT VALID;   -- VALIDATE later
```

The API maps `trashing` and `trashed` to `expired`, because users can't play either.

**Write path for derived columns.** This is required; without it, new calls are invisible to "today" pages.

- A `BEFORE INSERT OR UPDATE` trigger `calls_derive()` sets:
  - `local_day` and `local_hour` from the call's start time (`AT TIME ZONE 'Asia/Tashkent'`);
  - `client_phone_rev`;
  - `score10 = round(score/10.0, 1)`;
  - `reason_key = reason_key_of(<reason text>)`, where `reason_key_of` is a SQL function holding the mapping table.
- A second trigger (or the same one) inserts into `stats_dirty_days` when a row with `local_day < today` changes its status, score, duration, money or reason.
- Ingestion code sets `audio_path`, `audio_bytes`, `wav_path`/`wav_bytes` (if a WAV is kept), `audio_received_at = now()` at upload, and `peaks` (§8).
- Tests cover all of these for insert and update.

