### 6.3 Signals engine (rule-based, no LLM; thresholds from `company_settings.rules`)

It runs every 5 minutes during work hours, plus after `stats.changed` (debounced 60 s). It upserts today's signals (one per rule per company per day, via `dedupe_key`). A new or escalated signal also creates a notification.

The seed values below go into `default_company_settings.rules` and are copied per company. **They are data, not code.**

| Rule key | Condition (today, same window) | Severity | Metric shown | Target |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| short_spike | short ≥ `spikeMinCount` (20) and ≥ +`spikePct` (30)% vs the previous 7-day average | bad | "+34%" | audio?reason=short |
| no_answer_spike | the same test for no_answer | bad | "+x%" | audio?reason=no_answer |
| lagging_team | after `laggingAfterHour` (15), lagging ≥ `laggingTeamPct` (50)% of the team | bad | "10/12" | analytics?team=behind |
| quality_low | team average < target − `qualityGap` (2.0) | warn | "3.4" | staff?range=today |
| penalties_up / penalties_down | change ≥ `penaltyChangePct` (30)% and ≥ `penaltyMinCount` (3) vs yesterday | bad / good | "−56%" | audio?money=penalty |
| stt_paused | the circuit breaker is open | bad | "STT" | status (no date = today) |
| conversion_low | month-to-date conversion < `conversionWarnRatio` (0.7) × target | warn | "14.6%" | control |
| calls_up | calls ≥ +`callsUpPct` (20)% vs yesterday, same window | good | "+87%" | analytics |

Title and detail are `Msg`s with params. A detail lists up to 3 extensions plus "va yana {n} kishi". The control page returns the top 4, sorted by severity (bad → warn → good) and then by magnitude.

`rules` also holds `insightMinRated` (5), `weakestMinRated` (5) and `criterionFailPct` (50), used in §9 and §10.

