PATCH /company/norms Partial<Norms> & { confirm?: true } → Norms                     // owner/admin
      // lowering audioRetentionMonths without confirm: true → 409 { code: 'confirm_required' }
GET   /company/retention-preview?months=N → { months: number; toRemove: number; bytes: number; nextRunAt: ISODateTime }   // owner/admin
GET   /retention/status → RetentionStatus                                             // owner/admin/rop
interface RetentionStatus {
  months: number; mode: 'off' | 'dry_run' | 'live';        // this company's mode
  nextRunAt: ISODateTime;
  lastRun: { at: ISODateTime; mode: 'dry_run' | 'live'; removed: number; purged: number;
             bytesFreed: number; held: number } | null;
  audioAvailable: number;        // calls whose audio can still be played
  audioExpired: number;          // calls whose audio was removed, analysis kept
  expiringNext7Days: number;     // available, not kept, with expiresAt within 7 days
  expiringLink: DeepLink;        // an /audio link listing exactly those calls
  kept: number; keepLimit: number;
}
```

`expiresAt` for a call is the start time of the first nightly retention run (03:10 Tashkent) at which BOTH the call's day and the audio's arrival day are before `run date − audioRetentionMonths` (calendar months).

It is `null` when:
- the call is kept;
- the call is held (not final, see the backend spec §7.2);
- the company's retention mode is not `live`, or retention is globally disabled. In dry-run nothing is ever removed, so nothing is announced.

`expiringLink` is always a complete list link: `{ page: 'audio', params: { from: firstDataDay, to: today, audio: 'available', keep: 'false', expiringBefore: now + 7 days, sort: 'time_asc' } }`.

